[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-106412"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/c42f5aac98d31b7a66a60eebae34b5e83cb62f3ba4801595a81dd9bb57706384.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection/ecf39efdd97b81523287247fd7980e9afb50cd00685aa9cb02cdb82bca6a73a3" :answer/id #uuid "c1014d46-72b2-5674-8f29-021edef19c48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-6t,\\,\\,y=6{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection/d041ba44d7754b5898ca0cb6065e04a7cf638c8a6b1b4c0f72295da93613c86d" :answer/id #uuid "7e8d3bf6-e090-5df5-a794-98f8ba9231b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-t,\\,\\,y=-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection/97c2a6363be675a8998ebadfb8250c84faefd58913e1dc586fd6c80ef582d5a7" :answer/id #uuid "d2aaeaa2-a18b-5e77-a272-02c8cb810a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection/3c48307b04a2497304107f5a33113ed979922b85f07afa78270012f1f2e40eee" :answer/id #uuid "74f12e0f-e8b2-5911-bd0e-50b818fa3cab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3t,\\,\\,y=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection/395b3c84e69f0cb862f17c0edd073662d0661d453242220f6c3a61e578ac4a93" :answer/id #uuid "729bfb4b-e122-5a02-a844-4f165e3c7b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0af0c52-2abe-561e-947c-ce887d05910c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84673/selection/3c48307b04a2497304107f5a33113ed979922b85f07afa78270012f1f2e40eee" :answer-field/choices ["q-84673/selection/ecf39efdd97b81523287247fd7980e9afb50cd00685aa9cb02cdb82bca6a73a3" "q-84673/selection/d041ba44d7754b5898ca0cb6065e04a7cf638c8a6b1b4c0f72295da93613c86d" "q-84673/selection/97c2a6363be675a8998ebadfb8250c84faefd58913e1dc586fd6c80ef582d5a7" "q-84673/selection/3c48307b04a2497304107f5a33113ed979922b85f07afa78270012f1f2e40eee" "q-84673/selection/395b3c84e69f0cb862f17c0edd073662d0661d453242220f6c3a61e578ac4a93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84673" :question/id #uuid "c8369bdd-8409-5776-b1cd-08895b84e231" :question/math-academy-id "q-84673" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/237e807e6a36b3a6b5ac92fc3fa93d046761170ac2558511020ce382f70fd3c0.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(6,-6).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(6,-6),$ we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=-6$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6=2pt \\\\ -6=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =2pt \\\\ 3 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =p{(\\frac{3}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -6 & =p\\cdot \\frac{9}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{9}{p} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(-\\frac{3}{2})t,\\,y=(-\\frac{3}{2}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-3t,\\,y=-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84673/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7511fb86-dea4-5206-9ccd-69628a59473e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280209/field-1/fd9ca1cffa6c209ad15d1b41275c6e3e6bad8553b556d2cb6c937eaaac748dec" :answer/id #uuid "66bb59e0-0b5b-5164-bd40-f0fee88b366a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280209/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f65c54d0-936e-522a-bdb8-7755c98b8b51" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280209/field-1/fd9ca1cffa6c209ad15d1b41275c6e3e6bad8553b556d2cb6c937eaaac748dec" :answer-field/choices ["q-280209/field-1/fd9ca1cffa6c209ad15d1b41275c6e3e6bad8553b556d2cb6c937eaaac748dec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280209/field-2/e48a1bc5b0d32c90743d4d8bcb27ed2540e0b6d0a58aca35e3397ac96261b4a1" :answer/id #uuid "b5f50a61-b52e-595f-a829-f380f3897629" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280209/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "62da1243-ce30-514a-804d-f1f4c6c1156a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280209/field-2/e48a1bc5b0d32c90743d4d8bcb27ed2540e0b6d0a58aca35e3397ac96261b4a1" :answer-field/choices ["q-280209/field-2/e48a1bc5b0d32c90743d4d8bcb27ed2540e0b6d0a58aca35e3397ac96261b4a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280209" :question/id #uuid "b8e7fd54-cc70-5931-a4e3-d16151002a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280209" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/79609f38fef6121500dfc553137a6dd3af3a85ecd838a098c452748ab51ea13d.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the above parabola. Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-6,6),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-6=2pt \\\\ 6=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =2pt \\\\ -3 & =pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{3}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =p{(-\\frac{3}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 6 & =p\\cdot \\frac{9}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{9}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(\\frac{3}{2})t,\\,y=(\\frac{3}{2}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=3t,\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280209/field-1" "q-280209/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7511fb86-dea4-5206-9ccd-69628a59473e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210/field-1/fad1c1f465a41ebbc107311b8b4c37bc3966c4a0443843d15405174386287cfd" :answer/id #uuid "6ea81d68-8b7a-50c8-8bed-a514a0d13eb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210/field-1/1f18f819889926bfcc19b3ab684a349e64752633b940ad7097c8f6fdaf17887e" :answer/id #uuid "cc61aab1-4418-5b27-9b42-a81f50305e60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebbee884-d5e2-5168-8fea-d5073dc718ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280210/field-1/fad1c1f465a41ebbc107311b8b4c37bc3966c4a0443843d15405174386287cfd" :answer-field/choices ["q-280210/field-1/fad1c1f465a41ebbc107311b8b4c37bc3966c4a0443843d15405174386287cfd" "q-280210/field-1/1f18f819889926bfcc19b3ab684a349e64752633b940ad7097c8f6fdaf17887e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210/field-2/c1f843252a8583cc2b82f4be5f5293795eba547e6d13f7ecd0df6fbe2900eba7" :answer/id #uuid "75426c62-467a-5afd-8392-9af2ee415a5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4870d69-93b4-5290-a321-705f47bb4bcc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280210/field-2/c1f843252a8583cc2b82f4be5f5293795eba547e6d13f7ecd0df6fbe2900eba7" :answer-field/choices ["q-280210/field-2/c1f843252a8583cc2b82f4be5f5293795eba547e6d13f7ecd0df6fbe2900eba7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280210" :question/id #uuid "0c845806-ad5b-5436-a3d5-7e58cbbec065" :question/math-academy-id "q-280210" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/704181219623dc7269e7bcbb4de75c4181a5be4db3a097eb3d9da141dc64a403.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the above parabola. Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(10,5).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(10,5),$ we can substitute $x=10$ and $y=5$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10=2pt \\\\ 5=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =2pt \\\\ 5 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =p{(\\frac{5}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 5 & =p\\cdot \\frac{25}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{25}{p} \\\\ p & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(5)t,\\,y=(5){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=10t,\\,y=5{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280210/field-1" "q-280210/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7511fb86-dea4-5206-9ccd-69628a59473e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280226/field-1/072f782c0922d89ad7d5e700f086875781de3bf06bd3d0ccec87ca2e7afb1a35" :answer/id #uuid "0d4d193e-1ad7-5fcf-ac16-6bb379c93fff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280226/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe55af9-51c1-5991-9369-d12d55790a91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280226/field-1/072f782c0922d89ad7d5e700f086875781de3bf06bd3d0ccec87ca2e7afb1a35" :answer-field/choices ["q-280226/field-1/072f782c0922d89ad7d5e700f086875781de3bf06bd3d0ccec87ca2e7afb1a35"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280226/field-2/4779b744c6c2702d545b464ab0280ceb1fc21eb8e09f418fe409fde888ed4d63" :answer/id #uuid "21e8a7e7-06b5-599f-b6d8-622108988027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280226/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fefe99a7-0ff1-514f-9f69-963e98783e52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280226/field-2/4779b744c6c2702d545b464ab0280ceb1fc21eb8e09f418fe409fde888ed4d63" :answer-field/choices ["q-280226/field-2/4779b744c6c2702d545b464ab0280ceb1fc21eb8e09f418fe409fde888ed4d63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280226" :question/id #uuid "fe751547-4c45-5462-a7a1-024423d932ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-280226" :question/problem "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=32x.$ Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =32x \\\\ 4p & =32 \\\\ p & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(8){t}^{2},\\,y=2(8)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=8{t}^{2},\\,y=16t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280226/field-1" "q-280226/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c41ffe1b-e741-58bf-9844-83fbc6bc7030"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755/field-1/e9373628a8aa028817b563ea764550e3e776e7236efec469622843d0dd4809fb" :answer/id #uuid "134e073f-3d1b-5800-bae6-e53fd31a6a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755/field-1/c03fb218778a5a2982fb712d3f6a2922abc811bd32fcdcabbecbd42973296181" :answer/id #uuid "ecf92462-3fc8-5bad-af56-fa3683facda0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c43cf81-741b-5dbd-ac2f-299df4af5bc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274755/field-1/e9373628a8aa028817b563ea764550e3e776e7236efec469622843d0dd4809fb" :answer-field/choices ["q-274755/field-1/e9373628a8aa028817b563ea764550e3e776e7236efec469622843d0dd4809fb" "q-274755/field-1/c03fb218778a5a2982fb712d3f6a2922abc811bd32fcdcabbecbd42973296181"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755/field-2/27b9f22655ccf0b2d6755453458dea824e4c0dc7d52ad15a7b9beb5a52a87b8d" :answer/id #uuid "f32889c4-e261-5d80-b6d8-340aaee1bedf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e61122e-9c71-514c-9b53-fabfbed77748" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274755/field-2/27b9f22655ccf0b2d6755453458dea824e4c0dc7d52ad15a7b9beb5a52a87b8d" :answer-field/choices ["q-274755/field-2/27b9f22655ccf0b2d6755453458dea824e4c0dc7d52ad15a7b9beb5a52a87b8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274755" :question/id #uuid "dccd6f7f-a149-5a6a-8939-acec8e542598" :question/math-academy-id "q-274755" :question/problem "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=24x.$ Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =24x \\\\ 4p & =24 \\\\ p & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(6){t}^{2},\\,y=2(6)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=6{t}^{2},\\,y=12t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-274755/field-1" "q-274755/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c41ffe1b-e741-58bf-9844-83fbc6bc7030"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274755"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-280233"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/d8e4aa88acf2a0d69d4c4208dc4951a33cc92e59e177395ec74be3ae0f9a8c7f.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the parabola shown above. Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection/4f35b90bbb5bfecd2157f82e585a28591771adcaf0c968d1cf1df120071a259d" :answer/id #uuid "e9648099-e850-5fbc-b47f-bca7faaa16ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{16}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection/fcd8f3c5676133463d8d8727bb49458dcad767f60951621b55b0b5655bed6d3f" :answer/id #uuid "e5f0b71c-e4bd-552b-aeea-14c4fdf779ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{8}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection/572db1dd94784145ce1a287f821a06c62af73c523b6b35fc1877bc16cacf23cf" :answer/id #uuid "ac0e034d-0031-5fce-9eb1-12c0031be31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=8{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=16t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection/d5f6edfa02cafde28527b9906dbd4c7023f0f6ca7ad68dd07894f6072ec63dab" :answer/id #uuid "d7138c93-8e56-5813-b4aa-792350b0208d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=8{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection/4cf8c2af4893c6d06d6465fa90cfc1331fb2787c67dad2ad27919c162a005fb0" :answer/id #uuid "bcb94400-dd57-5b09-8e7f-910b97699f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{4}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d28120e2-a08f-5f8b-95af-21c31a5a869b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84719/selection/4cf8c2af4893c6d06d6465fa90cfc1331fb2787c67dad2ad27919c162a005fb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-84719/selection/4f35b90bbb5bfecd2157f82e585a28591771adcaf0c968d1cf1df120071a259d" "q-84719/selection/fcd8f3c5676133463d8d8727bb49458dcad767f60951621b55b0b5655bed6d3f" "q-84719/selection/572db1dd94784145ce1a287f821a06c62af73c523b6b35fc1877bc16cacf23cf" "q-84719/selection/d5f6edfa02cafde28527b9906dbd4c7023f0f6ca7ad68dd07894f6072ec63dab" "q-84719/selection/4cf8c2af4893c6d06d6465fa90cfc1331fb2787c67dad2ad27919c162a005fb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84719" :question/id #uuid "56c1507b-07af-5ef5-b091-f6c50ac855a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-84719" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/c8ec60cf31b66610fd9ddc8fc3fb8c30e8a27d2de41b6ecdeb358afa60588cf4.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(8,2).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(8,2),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=2$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 2=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 8 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(\\frac{1}{8}){t}^{2},\\,y=2(\\frac{1}{8})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2},\\,y=\\frac{1}{4}t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c41ffe1b-e741-58bf-9844-83fbc6bc7030"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280337/field-1/fbdb61a0b92923d59cc13e1bea1009356fc6f304af3b3e753467baa43398cacd" :answer/id #uuid "b64a9142-e4a9-5c18-9064-3ee9de13aa48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280337/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "88d7828e-a623-5953-b920-7d10d61af143" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280337/field-1/fbdb61a0b92923d59cc13e1bea1009356fc6f304af3b3e753467baa43398cacd" :answer-field/choices ["q-280337/field-1/fbdb61a0b92923d59cc13e1bea1009356fc6f304af3b3e753467baa43398cacd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280337" :question/id #uuid "d77dd31d-335e-5a60-b88d-a30ad6826051" :question/math-academy-id "q-280337" :question/problem "Consider the following parabola:\n\n$$\nx=4{t}^{2},\\,y=6t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the parabola is\n\n${y}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x}{4},\\,t=\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x}{4}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=9x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280337/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccc7f71-d2e0-5f35-80a5-042a53eda2da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280337"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" :answer/id #uuid "f5bc8864-4854-50e0-ab04-ffbb4637ea32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection/51f9c0e0b28c4d7e7ad94829c69c4ff4c5b96efc242224c78146ef16ecfebbc0" :answer/id #uuid "c142ead1-0a6d-5542-a04c-8db3b4e8f77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection/f7e2b4506bb6c8f1b5f22b9d8f12146b7c8411c18c9e10eb470616ac3abd122b" :answer/id #uuid "8fade18f-079e-5c1d-93c2-05e6ba815a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection/860826249f63e2e710924ee61bfe13806e1c2de2c49ecf55879bf018a65fddf0" :answer/id #uuid "bb7117b4-00c1-5b6c-a267-9390c1d9fcee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection/bee0ef55b953ebc03c79e2074a83df8414202f94b2ac7043220d384e29cc8e9c" :answer/id #uuid "e56c4328-3af9-5f8e-bb91-f0c63419aab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "875b6ea3-3843-55d2-9c29-32772ae7ae09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84734/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" :answer-field/choices ["q-84734/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" "q-84734/selection/51f9c0e0b28c4d7e7ad94829c69c4ff4c5b96efc242224c78146ef16ecfebbc0" "q-84734/selection/f7e2b4506bb6c8f1b5f22b9d8f12146b7c8411c18c9e10eb470616ac3abd122b" "q-84734/selection/860826249f63e2e710924ee61bfe13806e1c2de2c49ecf55879bf018a65fddf0" "q-84734/selection/bee0ef55b953ebc03c79e2074a83df8414202f94b2ac7043220d384e29cc8e9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84734" :question/id #uuid "6d723da4-6d35-5b58-905a-5236b3db4ebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-84734" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=-2{t}^{2},\\,y=-4t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-\\frac{x}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{y}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{x}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=-8x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84734/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccc7f71-d2e0-5f35-80a5-042a53eda2da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84734"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection/e0d10cc98c38a8d08d8d9c8846f46d5726bbb82b4ca89c3fc19833c4595b48cb" :answer/id #uuid "8be5a62e-8442-5404-b771-50ca6c0271a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{8}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" :answer/id #uuid "80dfda35-dc05-5f88-9248-0677f6cb8a02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection/1a25fa143b052b1bcd8ef371a372cc42309f86bafeec1b9b7e582070454ad508" :answer/id #uuid "dfcaa8b5-b930-5f37-a0c2-df9d7b3f6afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=12y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection/b97b2b0360b68e89267daec04b608dd52bb3d08d805b08054e729181046b55d1" :answer/id #uuid "f81c1289-421c-5521-bf88-bea86b19ec41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection/09dfa139565e3603a9f31d8f65aeab0ea89c5d8596eabadba3f26c1fa8f2d13a" :answer/id #uuid "4847fced-caaf-5469-bd8e-59974b22bc1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49196a48-8df7-5859-a98f-3671eb0a600d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84736/selection/b97b2b0360b68e89267daec04b608dd52bb3d08d805b08054e729181046b55d1" :answer-field/choices ["q-84736/selection/e0d10cc98c38a8d08d8d9c8846f46d5726bbb82b4ca89c3fc19833c4595b48cb" "q-84736/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" "q-84736/selection/1a25fa143b052b1bcd8ef371a372cc42309f86bafeec1b9b7e582070454ad508" "q-84736/selection/b97b2b0360b68e89267daec04b608dd52bb3d08d805b08054e729181046b55d1" "q-84736/selection/09dfa139565e3603a9f31d8f65aeab0ea89c5d8596eabadba3f26c1fa8f2d13a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84736" :question/id #uuid "2457959a-83fb-599c-9b5d-d9f0379d3f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-84736" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3t,\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\frac{x}{3},\\,{t}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}y$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{2}{3}y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${x}^{2}=6y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84736/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccc7f71-d2e0-5f35-80a5-042a53eda2da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-84731"] :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =4x,\\,t=2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =4{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=4x$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2} & =4x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7436"] :question/problem "What set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in(-\\infty, \\infty),$ generate the parabola shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039122/assets/0ae3d46a511cfe74b489eec33e6f6fec0adcb5be7d955a1880f979963b0e01f6.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
